<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: CZECH STATE BUDGET CZK 3.8BLN SURPLUS -END-JANUARY.</title>
<headline>CZECH STATE BUDGET CZK 3.8BLN SURPLUS -END-JANUARY.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1997-02-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Czech 1997 state budget recorded a 3.8 billion crown surplus for the month of January, the Finance Ministry said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The ministry said revenues totalled 43.1 billion crowns, while expenditures were 39.2 billion crowns.  </p>
<p> CZECH STATE BUDGET	 JAN 97     FY 96</p>
<p>  Revenue (CZK bln)	 43.066     482.8</p>
<p>  Expenditure		 39.230     484.3</p>
<p>  Balance		     +3.836    -1.562</p>
<p>Note. Comparative figures for January 1996 were not</p>
<p>immediately available.</p>
<p>-- Prague Newsroom, 42-2-2423-0003</p>
</text>
